---
const quoteMailto =
  "mailto:hello@mdquality.pl?subject=QA%20%2F%20Automation%20quote&body=Hi%20Miko%C5%82aj%2C%0A%0AProject%20or%20product%3A%0AWhat%20you%20need%20help%20with%3A%0ATimeline%3A%0AUseful%20links%20or%20context%3A%0A";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#080b10" />
    <title>Sample QA Release Readiness Report | MD Quality</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A fictional demonstration of a concise QA release-readiness report from MD Quality."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://mdquality.pl/sample-qa-report/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header>
      <nav class="container">
        <a class="logo" href="/">MD<span>Quality</span></a>
        <a class="back-link" href="/">Back to MD Quality</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="container">
      <section class="intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">DEMONSTRATION DELIVERABLE</p>
        <h1>Sample QA Release Readiness Report</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          This is a fictional example created only to show the structure and level of
          detail a client handover can contain. It is not a real client report and
          contains no client data.
        </p>

        <div class="notice">
          <strong>Example scenario</strong>
          <span>
            Fictional SaaS checkout release with web UI, account creation and payment API changes.
          </span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="report-section">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span>01</span>
          <div>
            <p>EXECUTIVE SUMMARY</p>
            <h2>Release recommendation: Conditional</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="label">OVERALL RISK</span>
            <strong>Medium</strong>
            <p>
              Core purchase flow works, but one payment retry defect should be resolved
              before the release is promoted to all users.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="label">BLOCKING ITEM</span>
            <strong>1 high-risk finding</strong>
            <p>
              Retrying a failed payment can create a duplicate order record in one edge case.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="label">RECOMMENDATION</span>
            <strong>Fix + targeted regression</strong>
            <p>
              Resolve the high-risk finding, rerun checkout regression and verify API idempotency.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="report-section">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span>02</span>
          <div>
            <p>SCOPE</p>
            <h2>What was checked</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="scope-grid">
          <div>
            <strong>Web flows</strong>
            <p>Guest checkout, registered checkout, account creation and order confirmation.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong>API behaviour</strong>
            <p>Payment request, retry handling, error responses and order status update.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong>Regression</strong>
            <p>Existing discount code, tax calculation, cart persistence and confirmation email.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <strong>Browsers</strong>
            <p>Current Chrome and Edge desktop plus a compact mobile viewport smoke check.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="report-section">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span>03</span>
          <div>
            <p>FINDINGS</p>
            <h2>Prioritized issues</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>ID</th>
                <th>Severity</th>
                <th>Area</th>
                <th>Finding</th>
                <th>Recommended action</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>QA-01</td>
                <td><span class="severity high">High</span></td>
                <td>Payments</td>
                <td>Retry after timeout can create a duplicate order record.</td>
                <td>Add idempotency protection and rerun retry-path regression.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>QA-02</td>
                <td><span class="severity medium">Medium</span></td>
                <td>Checkout UI</td>
                <td>Error message disappears after navigating back to payment step.</td>
                <td>Persist the validation state until the user changes payment data.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>QA-03</td>
                <td><span class="severity medium">Medium</span></td>
                <td>API</td>
                <td>One validation error returns a generic 500 instead of a 4xx response.</td>
                <td>Return a client-safe validation response and add an API regression check.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>QA-04</td>
                <td><span class="severity low">Low</span></td>
                <td>Mobile</td>
                <td>Order summary wraps awkwardly at a narrow viewport.</td>
                <td>Adjust responsive spacing before the next UI polish pass.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="report-section">
        <div class="section-title">
          <span>04</span>
          <div>
            <p>EVIDENCE & HANDOVER</p>
            <h2>What the client receives</h2>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="handover-grid">
          <article>
            <strong>Reproduction steps</strong>
            <p>Short, repeatable steps for each actionable finding.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <strong>Evidence</strong>
            <p>Screenshots, request/response samples or logs where they add value.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <strong>Risk notes</strong>
            <p>What is known, what remains uncertain and what should be retested.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <strong>Next actions</strong>
            <p>A prioritized list that makes the handover useful to developers and product owners.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="report-section decision">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">RELEASE DECISION</p>
          <h2>Proceed after QA-01 is fixed and the payment retry path passes regression.</h2>
          <p>
            Remaining medium and low findings can be accepted only if the product owner
            explicitly agrees to the documented risk.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a class="button" href={quoteMailto}>Request a QA / Automation Quote</a>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="container">
      <div class="logo">MD<span>Quality</span></div>
      <p>Fictional sample report · No client data</p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    font-family:
      Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont,
      "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 85% 5%, rgba(67, 140, 190, 0.12), transparent 28%),
      #080b10;
    color: #f4f7fb;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .container {
    width: min(1080px, calc(100% - 40px));
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  header {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #18212b;
    background: rgba(8, 11, 16, 0.9);
  }

  nav {
    min-height: 70px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .logo {
    color: white;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 850;
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: -0.6px;
  }

  .logo span {
    color: #7dd3fc;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: #9ba6b5;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: white;
  }

  .intro {
    padding: 95px 0 70px;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .section-title p,
  .label {
    color: #7dd3fc;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 850;
    letter-spacing: 1.6px;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 8px 0 22px;
    font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 72px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -3px;
  }

  .lead {
    max-width: 760px;
    color: #a5b0bd;
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  .notice {
    margin-top: 30px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border: 1px solid #2a3b4e;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #0c131b;
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .notice strong {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: #e7edf4;
  }

  .notice span {
    color: #8f9dae;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .report-section {
    padding: 72px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #18212b;
  }

  .section-title {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 42px 1fr;
    gap: 18px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 35px;
  }

  .section-title > span {
    color: #58697c;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 800;
    padding-top: 9px;
  }

  .section-title p {
    margin: 0 0 4px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 46px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -1.8px;
  }

  .summary-grid,
  .scope-grid,
  .handover-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .summary-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }

  .summary-grid article,
  .scope-grid > div,
  .handover-grid article {
    padding: 24px;
    border: 1px solid #1e2935;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #0d1219;
  }

  .summary-grid strong {
    display: block;
    margin: 6px 0 8px;
    font-size: 18px;
  }

  .summary-grid p,
  .scope-grid p,
  .handover-grid p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #8d9bac;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .scope-grid,
  .handover-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .scope-grid strong,
  .handover-grid strong {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 7px;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid #1e2935;
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    min-width: 780px;
    background: #0d1219;
  }

  th,
  td {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1b2430;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  th {
    color: #7f8da0;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  td {
    color: #aab5c2;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .severity {
    display: inline-block;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .severity.high {
    color: #ffb4b4;
    background: rgba(255, 88, 88, 0.1);
  }

  .severity.medium {
    color: #f7d78a;
    background: rgba(241, 184, 64, 0.1);
  }

  .severity.low {
    color: #9fd7f4;
    background: rgba(93, 180, 232, 0.1);
  }

  .decision {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 45px;
  }

  .decision > div {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .decision p:not(.eyebrow) {
    color: #8d9bac;
  }

  .button {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #f4f7fb;
    color: #080b10;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  footer {
    padding: 35px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #18212b;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    color: #667487;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .container {
      width: min(100% - 30px, 1080px);
    }

    .summary-grid,
    .scope-grid,
    .handover-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .notice,
    .decision {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .report-section {
      padding: 58px 0;
    }

    .button {
      width: 100%;
    }

    footer {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 8px;
    }
  }
</style>
